      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(runtime): guard JSON.stringify against circular references in tool output",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n\\`writeJson\\` and \\`writeRuntimeJson\\` call \\`JSON.stringify(value)\\` on arbitrary tool return values and model messages. If \\`value\\` contains circular references, \\`JSON.stringify\\` throws \\`TypeError: Converting circular structure to JSON\\`, crashing the output path with an unhandled exception.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrap both \\`JSON.stringify\\` calls in try-catch. On serialization failure, fall back to \\`JSON.stringify(String(value))\\` (which always succeeds).\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents runtime crashes when tools return objects with circular references. Output degrades gracefully to a string representation instead of crashing.",
